1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,725
Attackers do not guess one password at a time. They try millions, and they try leaked passwords from other sites.

2
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:16,145
Length beats complexity. Three or four random words make a long, memorable password.

3
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:28,200
Websites get breached. If you reuse a password, a breach on one site opens all your accounts, like one key for your house, car and office.

4
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:35,375
Check if your email appears in known breaches, and change any reused passwords now.

5
00:00:37,080 --> 00:00:45,330
A password manager is a safe for all your keys. You remember one strong password, it remembers the rest.

6
00:00:46,030 --> 00:00:54,955
Two-step sign-in adds a second lock: even a stolen password is not enough. Turn it on everywhere, especially email.

